From: fpvOS developers
Subject: [PATCH] ae: cap the exposure, the gain making up the rest

The vendor table lengthens the exposure to 10 ms before it raises the gain,
so indoors the sensor sits at 10 ms. --max-exposure-us N holds the exposure
at N and raises the gain by the same factor (exposure x gain, what the index
stands for, is kept) until the sensor is out of gain; the AE index stops
there. The noise ladders take the gain the sensor really runs at. The cap
comes before the anti-flicker snap, which only shortens the exposure to
whole mains half-periods and so stays within it.
--max-exposure-file PATH reads it from PATH instead, again on SIGHUP (as
the banding toggle), so a new cap applies live from the current index.

Upstream: not submitted

--- a/ml-aed/ml-aed.c
+++ b/ml-aed/ml-aed.c
@@ -92,6 +92,10 @@
